Declare the zlib requirement upstream's aws-sdk-cpp Conan recipe omits.

Upstream's 3.0 conanfile pins aws-sdk-cpp 1.11.842 from its own Conan remote
(recipe revision 363556887f622db23a10168c108dd55d). That recipe declares no
zlib requirement while aws-sdk-cpp enables zlib request compression whenever
CMake finds zlib: Conan 2 exposes the transitive zlib (via libcurl) to CMake
but hides its headers, so aws-cpp-sdk-core fails to compile on zlib.h.
Upstream's Ubuntu builder masks this with the system zlib1g-dev. This adds
the zlib requirement and the core component link that conan center's own
aws-sdk-cpp recipe carries. The package definition downloads the recipe,
applies this patch and re-exports it; the exported revision is the hash of
the recipe files, so the pin in internal/core/conanfile.py is reproducible.

Upstream recipe: https://milvus01.jfrog.io/artifactory/api/conan/default-conan-local2 (aws-sdk-cpp/1.11.842@milvus/dev)
Conan center recipe: https://github.com/conan-io/conan-center-index/blob/master/recipes/aws-sdk-cpp/all/conanfile.py

--- a/conanfile.py
+++ b/conanfile.py
@@ -380,6 +380,8 @@
         if self.settings.os != "Windows":
             self.requires("openssl/3.3.2")
             self.requires("libcurl/8.10.1")
+        # zlib is used if ENABLE_ZLIB_REQUEST_COMPRESSION is enabled, set ot ON by default
+        self.requires("zlib/[>=1.2.11 <2]")
         if self.settings.os in ["Linux", "FreeBSD"]:
             if self.options.get_safe("text-to-speech"):
                 self.requires("pulseaudio/14.2")
@@ -552,6 +554,7 @@
                 "aws-c-compression::aws-c-compression",
                 "aws-c-mqtt::aws-c-mqtt",
                 "aws-c-sdkutils::aws-c-sdkutils",
+                "zlib::zlib",
             ])
 
         # other components
